","scale":"linear","scaleNote":null,"gramsPerCup":null,"size":null,"optional":false,"aisle":"produce","pantry":false,"shop":true,"one":"fresh parsley"}],"steps":[{"text":"Slice each breast horizontally into two thin cutlets and press them to an even thickness. Season with the salt and pepper and dredge in the flour.","uses":[0,1,2,3]},{"text":"Heat the oil and 1 tbsp butter in the skillet over medium-high heat. Brown the cutlets in batches until golden and cooked through, {time 3 min} per side. Move to a plate.","uses":[4,5]},{"text":"Add the mushrooms to the pan and cook without stirring until browned underneath, {time 3 min}, then stir and cook until tender, {time 3 min}. Add the shallot and garlic for {time 1 min}.","uses":[6,7,8]},{"text":"Pour in the Marsala and scrape up the browned bits. Simmer until reduced by half, {time 3-4 min}, then add the broth and simmer until slightly thickened, {time 3 min}.","uses":[9,10]},{"text":"Off the heat, swirl in the remaining butter. Return the chicken and turn it in the sauce, then scatter with parsley. Serve with mashed potatoes or pasta.","uses":[11]}]}